/*
FILE : Strings.def
PROJECT : Omni360
DESCRIPTION : Every piece of text Omni360 shows, in English.

Each line is STR(ID, "English text"). Strings.h turns the IDs into an enum
and Strings.cpp turns the text into the built-in table, so a string is added
in exactly one place. English stays compiled in: it is what a translation
falls back to for any line it leaves out.

Text is UTF-8. Anything filled in at run time is a numbered placeholder -
{1} to {4} - never printf's %s or %d, so a translation can put the pieces
in whatever order its grammar wants. TrFormat fills them in.

Log lines stay in English and do not belong here.

Grouped by where the text appears; keep new lines with their screen.
*/

